## CAPABILITIES_REQUESTED

  KIND_USER(read)                — user identity the shell delegates to children.
  KIND_TTY(write)                — terminal render; children receive sub-caps.
  KIND_IPC_ENDPOINT(mint)        — pipeline pipe substrate; one mint per `|`.
  KIND_SHELL_SESSION(mint)       — session cap minted once per login; sub-caps per child.
  KIND_PDXFS_FILE(write)         — ~/.history/ CoW journal writes.

## SIGNING

  author_pk        paideia-os-team (ML-DSA-65, NIST L2)
                   fpr: <32-byte sha3-256; populated at release-signer bolt-on>
  paideia_root_pk  paideia_root_pk (ML-DSA-65, NIST L2; R32 root key)
                   fpr: <32-byte sha3-256; populated at release-signer bolt-on>

  Both fingerprints match what `pkg keys` reports on any
  paideia-os machine after `pkg install shell`. A mismatch means
  the shell binary reached the machine through an unattested
  path and `pkg install shell` should have refused it — file an
  incident and re-install from a verified mirror.
